\details{
The HiTOP-DAT (HiTOP Digital Assessment and Tracker) is a battery
of seven measures. This function scores 56 of the 57 scales in
\link{hitopdat_scales}: the WHODAS total, 18 IDAS-II scales, the AUDIT total,
the DUDIT total, CAPE positive symptoms, 33 CAT-PD facets and the PHQ-15
total. It returns raw scores, not T scores.

\strong{Scoring rules.} Each measure is scored on the metric of the source
named in its entry:
\itemize{
\item WHODAS: the sum of its 12 items, 0 to 48 (Andrews et al., 2009, p. 2).
\item IDAS-II: the sum of each scale's items, the metric of the norms in
Watson et al. (2012, Table 2).
\item AUDIT: the sum of its 10 items, 0 to 40 (Bergman & Källmén, 2002,
p. 245).
\item DUDIT: the sum of its 11 items, 0 to 44 (Berman et al., 2005, p. 23).
\item PHQ-15: the sum of the battery's 14 items, 0 to 28. The battery leaves
out the item on menstrual problems, as Hinz et al. (2017, p. 28) did.
\item CAT-PD facets: the mean of each facet's items, 1 to 5, the metric of the
CAT-PD scoring workbook the authors use. Reverse keys follow the IPIP
CAT-PD-SF key.
\item CAPE positive symptoms: the mean of its 20 items, 1 to 4, the metric of
the authors' REDCap version of the battery.
}

A reversed item scores the lowest plus the highest value of its answer
set, minus the answer.

\strong{Missing answers.} An \code{NA} answer is missing. A scale scores when the
share of its items answered is at least \code{min_complete}. A sum is then
prorated to the scale's full item count: the answered items' sum times
the item count, divided by the number answered. A mean is the answered
items' mean. A scale below \code{min_complete} scores \code{NA}. Each scale's
\verb{_complete} column holds its answered share, from 0 to 1. The battery's
authors chose this rule and its 80\% default. For the PHQ-15 it departs
from Hinz et al. (2017, p. 28), who filled one missing item with the
rounded mean of the other items and did not score a form with more
missing. This function prorates the PHQ-15 like the other sums, without
rounding.

\strong{General Depression.} The IDAS-II General Depression scale is not
scored, at the battery authors' request. Its row stays in
\link{hitopdat_scales} as a record of the IDAS-II key.

